    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: instruct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full; pending that review the fee is held and is neither collected nor refunded by the automated pipeline."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: on the driving facts this was a genuine, verified no-show, but the driver's own profile trips the anti-farming check, so the case cannot be paid out and must go to a human reviewer. The disputed amount (SGD 4.00) is held, not collected and not refunded, until that review finishes.\n\nWhy the fee is valid on the merits (POL-NS-01). All four limbs hold. (a) The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-09-08T09:30:20. (b) The GPS trace places the driver 24.0 m from the pickup pin, well inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius, from the first fix at 09:30:00 — before the arrived event. (c) The trace shows one continuous qualifying in-geofence run of 330 seconds, measured from the first in-geofence fix (09:30:00), against the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum — 30 seconds over, not under (shortfall_sec -30.0). (d) The driver terminated the trip at 09:35:30 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the dwell elapsed at 09:35:00.\n\nThe displacing clauses do not fire. POL-NS-02 confirms arrival (34 qualifying in-geofence fixes, no clock-skew issue). POL-NS-03 is about a driver stationary outside the arrival radius but within 400 m; here the driver was inside the radius at 24.0 m, so the wrong-entrance route is not engaged. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider: limb (a) fails because the chat log holds only the SYSTEM arrival notice and the driver's own 'Waiting at PLQ 3 pickup bay', nothing locating or coordinating from the rider, and limb (c) fails affirmatively — the rider track's 16 fixes sit at a mean 519 m from the pin, outside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE presence radius, with 0 qualifying fixes. POL-NS-05 does not bite: at the arrived timestamp the driver was 24.0 m from the pin (not over 300 m) and the trace records a single distinct speed of 0.0 km/h (not 15 km/h or more), so the arrival marker is genuine. POL-NS-06 does not apply: the effective dwell of 330 seconds exceeds the 300-second minimum, and its limb (i) could not be run in any case because the only traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09108-01) is MISSING, weight 0.0, and can carry no fact under POL-GEN-02.\n\nThe amount is correct. Under fee_schedule.resolution_rule the chargeable fee is the GREATER of the zone-class fee (LARGE_VENUE, SGD 4.00) and the vehicle-tier fee (RYDE_X, SGD 4.00), i.e. SGD 4.00, which is exactly the cancellation_fee line in the fare breakdown; there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect.\n\nWhy the outcome is ESCALATE, not a driver payout. POL-NS-07 would pay the driver 80 percent of the fee, SGD 3.20 of SGD 4.00 — but compensation is subject to the anti-farming check, and both its conjunctive limbs are met on driver_profile: no_show_terminations_30d is 7 (4 or more) and 7 divided by completed_trips_30d of 70 is 0.10, greater than 0.08. Compensation is therefore withheld and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d). The two driver-advocate claims that the withholding and the hold apply are accepted; the same claim's further assertion that the rider's refund demand is 'still refused at the pipeline level' is rejected — on escalation the fee is held, and POL-NS-07 directs the escalation packet to instruct the reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 in full, which is exactly what the rider's advocate argued and what the single referral records. The rider's claim that POL-NS-06 offers no relief on this trace is accepted, as is the rider's point that the abuse indicators here all run driver-side: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 (limb (d) needs 3 or more), and rider_profile and driver_profile disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0, so limb (c) is not met either. Under POL-GEN-01 the rider's lifetime prior_no_show_flags (1) is context only and carries no adverse finding; it was flagged for context and used for nothing.\n\nConfidence is 0.95. Every artifact that carries a deciding fact here — the GPS trace, the trip record, the fare breakdown and the driver profile — sits at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the cap is 1.0; the only impaired item (the missing advisory, weight 0.0) decides nothing. The escalation is compelled by POL-NS-07/POL-NS-09(d), not by the confidence floor of 0.70.",
