}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full; the disputed fee is held, not collected and not refunded, pending review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver — here is what the record shows and why no money is moved by the automated pipeline.\n\nThe trip itself is a verified no-show. The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-09-08T09:30:20 (POL-NS-01(a)). The GPS trace puts the driver about 24 m from the Paya Lebar Quarter PLQ 3 pin — far inside the 120 m arrival radius for this LARGE_VENUE pickup — from the first fix at 09:30:00, before the arrived event (POL-NS-01(b), POL-NS-02: 34 qualifying in-geofence fixes). He held position for one continuous run of 330 seconds against the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum (POL-NS-01(c)), and the trip was terminated by the driver at 09:35:30 on RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the dwell elapsed at 09:35:00 (POL-NS-01(d)). All four limbs hold. The SGD 4.00 line is also correct: the greater of the SGD 4.00 zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee is SGD 4.00, so there is no fare defect under POL-NS-08(d). The arrival marker was genuine (24 m from the pin at 0 km/h, so POL-NS-05 does not bite), and because the driver was inside the arrival radius, POL-NS-03's wrong-entrance route does not apply. The rider sent no locating or coordinating message and her device sits about 519 m from the pin, so POL-NS-04 does not exonerate her either.\n\nThe reason the case cannot be ruled financially is the driver's own profile. POL-NS-07's anti-farming check is conjunctive: no_show_terminations_30d of 4 or more AND that figure divided by completed_trips_30d greater than 0.08. The record shows 7 terminations in the trailing 30 days and 70 completed trips — 7 ÷ 70 = 0.10. Both limbs are satisfied, so the driver's compensation (80 percent of the fee, SGD 3.20 of SGD 4.00) is withheld and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d).\n\nEscalation is terminal: no monetary ruling issues, and the disputed SGD 4.00 is held — neither collected from the rider nor refunded — until a human reviewer resolves the driver's pattern. The escalation packet directs the reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full.\n\nTwo supporting points. The traffic advisory for this pickup, EV-ADVIS-09108-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and can carry no fact, so POL-NS-06(i) cannot be run — and the rider did not press a dwell shortfall in any event. And the lifetime prior_no_show_flags field is context only under POL-GEN-01; it is not the trailing-30-day counter POL-NS-09(d) reads."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: the escalation packet must direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full; the disputed SGD 4.00 is held, neither collected nor refunded, while review is pending."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is chargeable on the merits of this trip, but the driver's own profile forces the case to a human reviewer, so no money moves through the automated pipeline today.\n\nRider — your claim that the charge itself is improper fails on the record. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold. (a) The trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 2026-09-08T09:30:20. (b) The GPS trace places the driver 24.0 m from the pickup pin — well inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius — from the first fix at 09:30:00, i.e. before the arrival event; the 34 in-geofence fixes satisfy POL-NS-02 with no accuracy-filtering problem. (c) The trace shows one continuous qualifying in-geofence run of 330 seconds, exceeding the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum, measured from the first qualifying fix and not from the arrival tap. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 09:35:30 on RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three recognised codes, after the 300-second minimum elapsed at 09:35:00. The amount is also correct: under fee_schedule.resolution_rule the chargeable fee is the GREATER of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), so SGD 4.00, which is exactly the cancellation_fee line in the fare breakdown (no POL-NS-08(d) defect).\n\nYour alternative routes are closed. POL-NS-06 gives you nothing: a 330-second dwell exceeds the minimum, so there is no shortfall (shortfall_sec is −30.0), and the only route to accumulating further in-geofence time, POL-NS-06(i), cannot be run because the sole traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-09108-01, is MISSING, carries no payload and, at weight 0.0 (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), can carry no fact under POL-GEN-02. POL-NS-05 does not bite: at the arrival timestamp the driver was 24.0 m from the pin and the trace records a single distinct speed of 0.0 km/h, so the marker is genuine and the waiting clock is not recomputed. POL-NS-03 does not apply: that clause governs a driver stationary outside the arrival radius but within 400 m, whereas this driver was inside the radius throughout. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate you: the chat log holds only two messages — the SYSTEM arrival notice and the driver's own 'Waiting at PLQ 3 pickup bay' — so you sent nothing locating or coordinating (limb (a) fails), and your rider track holds 16 fixes at a mean 519 m from the pin with 0 qualifying fixes inside the 150 m rider-presence radius (limb (c) fails affirmatively).\n\nDriver — the fee stands, but your compensation is not paid today. POL-NS-07 would compensate you SGD 3.20 (80 percent of SGD 4.00), but its anti-farming check trips on both conjunctive limbs: no_show_terminations_30d is 7 (4 or more) and 7 divided by completed_trips_30d of 70 is 0.10, above the 0.08 threshold. Compensation is therefore withheld and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d).\n\nOn the pattern you asked about: the rider-side abuse indicators are clean — no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and both disputes_with_counterparty_90d figures are 0, so POL-NS-09(c) and the rider-side half of (d) do not fire. The escalation rests entirely on the driver's own trailing-30-day figures, cited under POL-NS-07 and POL-NS-09(d), which POL-GEN-01 permits. No other profile field — the lifetime prior_no_show_flags, rating, account age, cancellation rate and the rest — is used as a ground against either party; those are context only.\n\nESCALATE is terminal: no monetary ruling issues, amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd are null, and the disputed SGD 4.00 is held rather than collected or refunded while review is pending. Open question for the reviewer: whether this driver's trailing-30-day no-show terminations reflect a repeat fee-farming pattern — on which the packet carries POL-NS-07's standing instruction to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 in full."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07 (anti-farming branch): direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full."
